<section data-l="en"><h1>Field Ops — Privacy Policy</h1>
<div class="updated">Last updated: October 6, 2026</div>
<div class="hl">Field Ops is built to work locally, on your phone. Your data leaves your phone only when you explicitly choose (cloud backup, export, sharing, Pro subscription). On Android, in the free version, the app shows ads through Google AdMob (see section 5); the Pro subscription removes ads. We do not sell your personal data.</div>
<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>Field Ops is developed by Gioroc Horatiu, referred to below as &quot;we&quot; or &quot;the developer&quot;. For any question related to privacy, you can contact us at the address in the Contact section, at the end of this document.</p>
<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
<h3>Data stored locally, on your phone</h3>
<ul><li>Points of interest — name, type, GPS coordinates, description, photos</li><li>Routes and tracks created or recorded (including &quot;Merge&quot;)</li><li>Distance and area measurements</li><li>Freehand drawings created on the map</li><li>Personal profile — name, rank, role, unit, photo (all optional)</li><li>Display preferences (including the MGRS grid) and downloaded offline maps</li></ul>
<h3>Location data (GPS)</h3>
<p>We use the device&#x27;s location for the app&#x27;s core features: map, navigation, distance calculations, track recording. Your precise location is used only on-device, unless you explicitly choose a cloud backup.</p>
<h3>Photos and camera</h3>
<p>We access the camera/gallery only with your explicit permission. Photos remain local unless you include them in a backup or export you initiate.</p>
<h3>Account data (Cloud Backup)</h3>
<p>If you enable cloud backup: email and password (securely managed by our infrastructure provider).</p>
<h3>Data related to your Pro subscription</h3>
<p>If you purchase Field Ops Pro, payment is handled entirely by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play) — we never receive or store your payment details. We only receive an anonymous device identifier and your subscription status (active/expired/cancelled), through our provider RevenueCat.</p>
<h3>Advertising data (Android free version only)</h3>
<p>Ads are shown through Google AdMob (Google Mobile Ads SDK). Google may collect and use device identifiers (for example the Android advertising ID), IP address, device and app information, and approximate location, to serve and measure ads and to prevent abuse. We do not send the points, routes, photos or profile you save in the app to the ad provider.</p>
<h3>OpenStreetMap maps and place search</h3>
<p>When you use the OpenStreetMap (OSM) map, download offline maps or search for a place, your device sends requests directly to the OpenStreetMap servers (tile.openstreetmap.org) and Nominatim (nominatim.openstreetmap.org). These servers receive your IP address, the app identification, the requested map areas and, for search, the text you typed. We do not send them your points, routes, photos or profile. The OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy: osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy.</p>
<h2>3. Cloud Backup (optional)</h2>
<p>Optional feature, disabled by default. When you press &quot;Backup now&quot;, we send your points, routes, measurements, Merge tracks, drawings, and profile, strictly tied to your account — fully isolated from other users. You can delete the backup at any time, directly from the app.</p>
<h2>4. Third-party providers involved</h2>
<ul><li>Apple Maps — native map on iOS</li><li>Google Maps — native map on Android</li><li>OpenStreetMap — OSM maps and offline download</li><li>Nominatim — place search for offline maps</li><li>Supabase — cloud infrastructure for authentication and backup</li><li>RevenueCat — Pro subscription management, without access to your payment details</li><li>Apple App Store / Google Play — payment processing</li><li>Google AdMob — ads, on Android in the free version only</li></ul>
<h2>5. Ads and consent</h2>
<p>Ads appear only on Android, only in the free version, on secondary screens (not on the main map). Pro users do not see ads.</p>
<p>In the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, before showing ads we ask for your consent through a Google form, as required by law. You may decline; ads may then be limited or non-personalized.</p>
<p>You can reset or delete your advertising ID in Android settings (Settings → Google → Ads, or Privacy → Ads), and you can see how Google uses data at policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites.</p>
<h2>6. Data security</h2>
<ul><li>Local data stored in the app&#x27;s private storage</li><li>Cloud backup protected by authentication and strict access rules</li><li>Encrypted communication (HTTPS/TLS)</li></ul>
<h2>7. Your control and rights</h2>
<ul><li>Trash — restore within 30 days, then automatic permanent deletion</li><li>Delete cloud backup, anytime</li><li>&quot;Delete all data&quot; — permanently deletes data on your phone</li><li>Kill Switch — complete, irreversible reset, with explicit confirmation</li><li>Subscription management — you can cancel automatic renewal anytime, from your Apple/Google account settings</li><li>If you are in the EU/EEA or the UK you have the right of access, rectification, erasure, portability and objection for the data we store (cloud backup); write to us at the contact address</li></ul>
<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>Field Ops is not intended for children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect data from children under this age.</p>
<h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy periodically. Any significant change will be reflected by updating the date above.</p>
<h2>10. Contact</h2><p>For any question related to privacy: <a href="mailto:horatiu.gioroc@gmail.com">horatiu.gioroc@gmail.com</a></p>
